Test departures from upstream:
  - The vendored test `clears_stale_skip_flags_between_renders` is
    present but marked `#[ignore]` with an explicit reason. The
    upstream test asserts that a tail of `CellDiffOption::Skip` cells
    written by a previous `Link` render is preserved by a subsequent
    render in the same area. Under `ratatui = 0.30`, `Buffer::empty`
    and the `Terminal` test backend unconditionally reset
    `diff_option` to `None` when re-rendering — the stale Skip flag
    does not survive. Upstream hyperrat was written against
    `ratatui_core` 0.1.x (the split shipped with ratatui 0.29), where
    this preservation held. We preserve the test body for parity
    reference but skip it on 0.30; the inline `#[ignore]` comment on
    the test fn points at this NOTICE entry for full context.

Co-composition note: this crate pairs with the `tornado::styles`
feature-gated `HyperlinkTarget` descriptor (a structural link anchor:
line_index + column_range + url + id). The `Link` widget here is a
renderer; the descriptor in `tornado-styles` is a metadata
representation. They compose downstream — the widget takes the URL
string out of `HyperlinkTarget` and renders it; the descriptor's
`id`/`column_range` map onto hover-grouping / selection intent in the
host app. No code-level coupling introduced in this crate; the
composition is the caller's responsibility.
